IO-51: force the continuity tables on large negative errors too

massbal_report() writes a continuity table when [REPORT] CONTINUITY is YES
or when the error exceeds 10 %, but compares the signed error, so a large
negative error (more water or mass leaving or stored than came in) never
forces the table. Compare the magnitude instead, and make
massbal_getLoadingError() return the error of largest magnitude, as
massbal_getQualError() does, instead of the largest positive one.

Requires: IO-50

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b,
after IO-50_swmm530.patch:
    git apply IO-51_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/massbal.c b/src/legacy/engine/massbal.c
index 48266c2..fe48892 100644
